---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";

const sections = [
  ["introduction", "Introduction"],
  ["software", "Open-source software in Modesto"],
  ["providers", "Coding-agent providers you connect"],
  ["trademarks", "Names and trademarks"],
  ["notices", "Full notices"],
  ["contact", "Contact us"],
] as const;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Third Party — Modesto"
  description="Open-source notices, provider trademarks, and third-party software Modesto depends on."
  heading="Third Party"
  lede="Modesto is built on other people’s work and connects to tools you already use. This page explains those relationships: the open-source software shipped with Modesto, the coding-agent providers you choose, and where the full license notices live."
  effectiveDate="2026-09-08"
  lastUpdated="2026-09-12"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="introduction">
    <p class="section-number">01</p>
    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      Modesto includes and depends on third-party open-source software, and it can talk to
      third-party coding agents, model providers, identity services, and infrastructure that you
      install or authenticate yourself. This notice describes those two different kinds of
      “third party,” because they are easy to confuse and they have different privacy and
      licensing consequences.
    </p>
    <p>
      Software we ship with Modesto is subject to the licenses of those projects. The App itself is
      AGPL-3.0 because it bundles the Bible Strong avatar engine; see the repository{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto/blob/main/LICENSE">LICENSE</a> and{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md"
        >third-party notices</a
      >. Services you connect at runtime are subject to those services’ own terms. We do not claim
      ownership of either. Our{" "}<a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> and{" "}<a href="/terms-of-service"
        >Terms of Service</a
      >{" "}explain how that split works for data and liability.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="software">
    <p class="section-number">02</p>
    <h2>Open-Source Software in Modesto</h2>
    <p>
      The authoritative inventory of third-party packages is the workspace <code>package.json</code>
      files and <code>bun.lock</code> in the{" "}<a href="https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto"
        >Modesto repository</a
      >. Each dependency remains subject to its own license and copyright notices. Do not treat
      this page as a substitute for those texts.
    </p>
    <p>Major runtime and tooling dependencies include, among others:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>@bible-strong/avatar-core and @bible-strong/avatar-react — AGPL-3.0-only</li>
      <li>React and React DOM — MIT</li>
      <li>Electron — MIT</li>
      <li>Vite — MIT</li>
      <li>TanStack Router, Query, Virtual, and Pacer — MIT</li>
      <li>Effect and Effect platform packages — MIT</li>
      <li>Tailwind CSS — MIT</li>
      <li>Base UI — MIT</li>
      <li>xterm.js packages — MIT</li>
      <li>Astro — MIT</li>
      <li>Vitest — MIT</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This list is a convenience summary. License texts distributed by each project control if
      there is any conflict with this page. Original copyright and license notices for
      third-party code must not be removed. If code is adapted from another project, the source,
      license, and nature of the adaptation are recorded in the repository’s third-party notices.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="providers">
    <p class="section-number">03</p>
    <h2>Coding-Agent Providers You Connect</h2>
    <p>
      Modesto is a harness, not a model host. When you install and sign in to Codex, Claude Code,
      Cursor Agent, Gemini CLI, Grok, Meta (Muse Code / Muse Spark), Factory Droid, Kilo,
      OpenCode, Pi, or another supported provider, you are using that provider’s software and
      accounts. Prompts, files, and related context you send leave your machine on that
      provider’s terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not endorse a provider by listing it. We do not control a provider’s uptime, pricing,
      retention, training practices, or output quality. Review each provider’s terms, privacy
      policy, and data-control settings before you send it confidential, proprietary, regulated,
      or personal information. Disconnecting a provider in Modesto does not delete data that
      provider already received; you must use that provider’s own tools.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some providers are reached through locally installed CLIs, SDKs, or protocols such as ACP.
      Those binaries are not Modesto, even when the App launches or detects them. Their licenses
      and security properties are the provider’s.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="trademarks">
    <p class="section-number">04</p>
    <h2>Names and Trademarks</h2>
    <p>
      Provider names, logos, and trademarks belong to their respective owners. Listing a
      provider, showing its mark in the App or on the Site, or describing an integration is not a
      claim that Modesto is affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by that owner, and it is
      not a claim that we copied that owner’s product.
    </p>
    <p>
      Connections tiles, composer mentions, and similar pickers show third-party product marks
      (Gmail, Slack, Figma, Higgsfield, Canva, Supabase, and others) so you can recognise apps you
      already use. Most of those SVG paths come from{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/simple-icons/simple-icons">Simple Icons</a> (CC0). Official
      geometry is used where a mark is only recognisable in its published form. The marks remain
      the owners’ trademarks.
    </p>
    <p>
      OpenAI Codex, Claude, Cursor, Gemini, Grok, Meta, Factory, Kilo, OpenCode, Pi, Cline,
      Continue, T3 Code, and Codex Monitor are among the ecosystem names you may see in Modesto
      or in our documentation. They are used to identify compatible tools and references. The
      Modesto name, Handoff Mark, and related brand assets are described on the{" "}<a
        href="/branding">Branding</a
      >{" "}page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="notices">
    <p class="section-number">05</p>
    <h2>Full Notices</h2>
    <p>
      The complete third-party notice file, including additional attributions such as artwork
      licenses, lives in the repository:
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md"
        >github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md</a
      >
    </p>
    <p>
      If you believe a required notice is missing or incorrect, open an issue or pull request on
      that file. Architectural or design inspiration is acknowledged separately and is not
      described as copied code without evidence.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <p class="section-number">06</p>
    <h2>Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about third-party notices, attribution, or provider listings can be sent through
      the public repository:
    </p>
    <address>
      <strong>Modesto</strong><br />
      Tanner Davidson<br />
      <a href="https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto">github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto</a>
    </address>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
